In article <d9acb640.0209250716.78ff33ec@posting.google.com> julian.daly@astrium-space.com (Julian Daly) writes:
>ld:
>io.mod: branch relocation out-of-range, bad object file produced,
>can't branch from 0xfffffc000024882c to 0xfffffc00006910ec
>Relinking with trampoline code
>chmod 755 a.out
>(null command)
>mv a.out vmunix.sys
>ln vmunix.sys vmunix; ln vmunix vmunix.SYSNAME
>
>Can anyone please explain why we are seeing this and how we can fix it?

There is nothing to fix. The link worked successfully. The message
is merely a "warning" that your kernel was big enough to require
trampoline code (extra jumps) to get at branch targets too far away.

The warning message has been suppressed in V5.0 and later, since it
is of pretty much no consequence.

As long as the relink worked, you are all set.

