"Mike Elleby" <mikemillion@earthlink.net> wrote in message news:<oitk9.3494$u56.283489@newsread1.prod.itd.earthlink.net>...
> Can this be done.  I've seen several threads on dual booting NT and UNIX,
> and diffent versions of UNIX on the same machine, but can this same thing be
> done with VMS and UNIX?
> 
> Thanx.
> 
> Mike Elleby

yes, assuming you use different physical disk for each OS.
you will only use the SRM console.

assuming your unix disk id dka0 and you OpenVMS disk is dkb100

to boot unix :
P00>>set os_type Unix
P00>>boot -fl a dka0

to boot OpenVMS

P00>>set os_type openvms
P00>>boot -fl 0,0 dkb100 

of course, *avoid* accessing vms disks from unix and vice versa.


Cheers,

Emmanuel


