If you want to start sys_check -escalate from a script at boot-time you need
to do
the following:

1) maked sure crashdc(savecore) has run before you start your script.
2)find out if crashdc(savecore) has created a new /var/adm/crash/vmzcore.n
2bis) store 'n' in a variable eg BOUNDS. If there is no vmzcore to save
         set BOUNDS=none
3)define TMPDIR=/mymount/mydir  (eg /var/tmp)
4)launch sys_check with "/usr/sbin/sys_check -escalate $BOUNDS"

For an example on how to run sys_check from scripts, check
/usr/share/sysman/bin/runsyscheck

Johan Brusche.




