Julian:
  This error can be caused by one of two things.

  1) Look closely to see if you missed a linker error reporting an
     unresolved symbol.  If you see one, fix that first and this
     error should go away.  Based on your output, I doubt that is 
     what is happening, but you should check it.

  2) The more likely cause of the problem is that the kernel you 
     are linking has a .text section size larger than 8 megabytes.
     This "8 meg" limit was lifted in the V5.1 release but exists
     in all earlier releases.  The only solution is to reduce the
     the amount of kernel code you are linking with.  One way
     is to select less options on the doconfig menu.  Another way,
     if you are linking in your own kernel modules, is to load them
     as dymanic loadable modules so that they're not linked into
     your vmunix.

Joe Mario
HP Tru64 UNIX Development Environment Group


