Fabien R wrote:
> 
> Hi all,
> 
> I have a PWS500au and the CMOS battery is down. I updated the bios
> advanced cmos settings by choosing UNIX SRM and rebooted. But the
> system can't boot because no OS are found.
> Is it possible to specify manually which system to choose and how ?
> 
> Thanks in advance,
> Fabien

You must set some console environment variables:

set bootdef_dev dkxxx    # your boot device
set boot_file vmunix	 # vmunix or genvmunix ...
det boot_osflags a	 # a = multiuser or s = single user mode

and optional

set auto_action boot  	 # automatic reboot after a crash/reset
or 
set auto_action halt	 # system halts in SRM console mode after a
crash/reset

I think thats all, then you can type 
>>> boot

