Did you stop the process?  Removing a file's name doesn't cause
the space to be freed if something has the file open or there are
other names for the file (hard links).  As someone else suggested
use lsof (or fuser) to see if the file is still open.

>I betcha a reboot will give our space back but thats not a conveniant
>thing to do.

Killing the process will be sufficient.  A reboot will certainly
do that, but it is more than necessary.

>We will suffer along with 512Mb free but that will only keep us going
>a day or so.
