The file still being open is the usual cause of space apparently
not being freed when a file is removed.  If you're using UFS I
can't think of any other cause for the symtom.  AdvFS is another
matter.

I'm told that AdvFS is dependent on its quota system to keep track
of the space being used.  If you're not using the quota system (even
if it isn't enforcing them), it seems to be quite easy to get the
actual space usage out of sync with what the file system thinks is
being used.  This symtoms shows up a difference in space usage
between df(1) and what the file systems tools think is in use;
showfdmn.  Running quotacheck on the domain may be enough to fix
it.


