The binary event log is /var/adm/binary.errlog.  However as the name
and description suggest, it is binary data.  On many V4 and older
systems uerf(8) will format the log.  You'll want to use the option
"-o full" to get the full event listing, since the default level
of formatting merely tells you there was event for SCSI errors
and offers little detail.  The "-o full" output will give the
module logging the event, some extra description, the SCSI CDB
that generated the error and when present the SCSI Request Sense
data for the error.

Some V4 systems changed the format of the data and uerf(8) can't
format it.  On these you need DECevent (dia).  The kit for DECevent
is on one of the Associated Product CDROMs.  The web site for
the Service organization (www.services.compaq.com) will have the
most current version of the kit somewhere.

Compaq Analyze can also do translation of the binary event log
to text.  It is part of the WEBES kit, also on the Associated
Product CDROMs.

