Go to the AlphaBios prompt, F1 during boot up I think, and set the OS type to UNIX.
Save the entry, and hit the RESET button, do not power the machine off yet.
The system will reboot to the SRM console (the blue screen with the >>> prompt).

You must set some console environment variables, the way to do this is type commands
at the >>> prompt.
The first one should be:
    set os_type unix
this will set the operating system type to UNIX and will load the SRM, not the
AlphaBios, every time you boot the system.

Additional variables will need to be set and are generally set by the install
utility.

I would suggest that the auto_action be set to   HALT   until you get things the way
you want them.  When the system comes up from a cold boot or crashes it will come up
to the SRM prompt  >>> then you can adjust thing as needed.

You can check your settings by doing   >>> show os_type or show auto_action and you
should have the following settings.
>>> os_type unix
>>> set auto_action halt

The following URL points to a version of the SRM manual that may provide additional
help.

http://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/info/semiconductor/literature/srmcons.pdf

Good luck,
E.Paul

