I think the psrinfo command with the -v option will do what
you want:

% psrinfo -v
Status of processor 0 as of: 09/05/02 17:02:53
  Processor has been on-line since 09/05/2002 15:53:45
  The alpha EV5.6 (21164A) processor operates at 532 MHz,
        and has an alpha internal floating point processor.
Status of processor 1 as of: 09/05/02 17:02:53
  Processor has been on-line since 09/05/2002 15:53:45
  The alpha EV5.6 (21164A) processor operates at 532 MHz,
        and has an alpha internal floating point processor.

This was from a dual CPU AlphaServer 1200.  I tried it on a
V3.2C DEC 3000 Model 500 and the result were less informative,
so your results will vary depending the age of the operating
system and/or system.

