you want to run it any other time? Sys_check does not (or would you want it)
have to be running when the system crashes. Support takes the data from the
sys_check -escalate (that's to do an engineering escalation) and finds out
why it crashed and gets a patch (if you are under service and the OS version
is supported) or calls out the failing hardware. I do this 5 days a week and
it's not hard.

